  "theorem": {
    "candidate_and_verification_cost": "The true pair output is O(K) up to the constant 20 occurrence splits per planted C6 source; independent uniform unplanted targets contribute the same n^2N/q expected scale to the true orientation as to the false one. Total candidate roots are therefore B^(3/4+o(1)) in expectation. Scanning N target labels per candidate costs B^2 and removes every opposite-sign-only root exactly. Markov gives a B^(3/4+epsilon) candidate cap except with probability B^(-epsilon).",
